# Note Structure Rules

## Topic Layout

Each topic should follow:

```text
notes/<topic>/
├── <topic>-notes.tex
├── compile.sh
├── progress.json
├── chapters/
│   ├── chapter0.tex
│   └── chapterN.tex
└── appendix/
    └── qa.tex
```

## Chapter Notes

- `chapter0.tex` is the literature overview and learning map.
- Later chapters should be motivation-first: introduce examples or problems before abstract definitions when possible.
- Detailed derivations belong in the appendix, with a正文 footnote pointing to `\cref{...}`.
- Keep each chapter independently readable, but integrate through the topic master file.

## Progress Tracking

- Update `progress.json` or the topic progress file when reading status changes.
- Do not rewrite `appendix/qa.tex` wholesale. It is a high-value archive.
